      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: AGRICULTURE – BASIC CONCEPT & ROLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian agriculture is structured around three major cropping seasons: Kharif, Rabi, and Zaid.",
        "Agricultural practices vary from subsistence and intensive farming to commercial and plantation systems.",
        "Staple food crops like Rice and Wheat, alongside coarse grains, millets, and cash crops, form the backbone of Indian agrarian production.",
        "The Green Revolution brought structural transformation and high yields, along with specific economic and ecological limitations.",
        "Irrigation infrastructure and climatic/soil requirements are critical determinants of crop distribution across Indian states."
      ],
      "id": "m77omh9"
    },
